# Local CI gate (required before push)

GitHub CI is defined in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. **Do not push** if local CI fails.

## Required command (same gates as GitHub)

```bash
./scripts/ci-local.sh
```

Runs: `uv sync --frozen`, ruff, mypy, pytest+coverage, Docker builds (api, worker, catalog).

## Pre-push hook

After clone or when hooks are missing:

```bash
chmod +x scripts/*.sh scripts/git-hooks/*
./scripts/install-git-hooks.sh
```

The **pre-push** hook runs `ci-local.sh` and **rejects the push** on any failure.

## Agent rules

- Before `git push`, run `./scripts/ci-local.sh` and fix all errors.
- **Never** suggest `git push --no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests bypassing hooks.
- **Never** push broken code to let GitHub fail; local CI must pass first.
